// Brought to u by MidManStudio
// FILE: .mdix/replacements/replacements.mdix
//
// Replacement set: the `query2_static` 4x investigation.
//
// Six files, delivered as one archive (`mid-ecs-abi-fix.tar.gz`) sitting
// next to this manifest — the mobile path. Commit two files through the
// GitHub web UI (this manifest and the archive), run
// `.github/workflows/run-replacements.yml`, done. No local shell needed,
// no six-file web-UI editing session on a 2141-line source file.
//
// WHAT THIS CHANGES
//
//   Cargo.toml                                (workspace member added)
//   crates/mid-ecs/src/archetype.rs           (Iter1/Iter2 moved out; `mod iter;`)
//   crates/mid-ecs/src/archetype/iter.rs      (NEW — all query iterators)
//   crates/mid-ecs/src/query.rs               (query_static_ref/query2_static_ref)
//   benches/abi-return-size/Cargo.toml        (NEW)
//   benches/abi-return-size/benches/abi_return_size.rs  (NEW)
//
// Nothing else in the workspace is touched. `Iter1`/`Iter2` keep their
// exact public behaviour and item types — every existing caller, test
// and bench compiles and behaves unchanged. The new `_ref` methods are
// purely additive.
//
// ORDER OF OPERATIONS — do not skip step 1
//
//   1. Run `benches/abi-return-size` first. It links against NOTHING
//      (no mid-ecs, no bevy_ecs) precisely so it cannot be tipped by
//      mid-ecs's own compilation-unit layout the way archetype_core.rs's
//      controls were in builds #15-#18. Its `ret16_ref_ref` group is the
//      control that separates "item size" from "reads a second column" —
//      a distinction every diagnostic so far has had confounded.
//   2. Only then read `query2_static_ref` against `query2_static`.
//
//   If `ret16_ref_ref` lands with `ret24_entity_ref_ref` rather than with
//   `raw_two_field`, the ABI hypothesis is dead and `query2_static_ref`
//   is just an API convenience. That outcome is a genuinely useful
//   negative and should be written up in docs/mid-ecs.md the same way
//   the seven before it were.
//
// DRY RUN FIRST
//
//   run-replacements.yml defaults `dry_run` to 'true' on manual
//   dispatch. Leave it there for the first run and read the diff —
//   archetype.rs is a real edit to a real 2141-line file, not a new
//   file, and it is the one entry here worth eyeballing before writing.
//   Note the push trigger on `.mdix/replacements/**` also defaults to a
//   dry run, so committing these two files does not itself write
//   anything.
//
// THE ROOT Cargo.toml IS DELIBERATELY NAMED `ROOT_Cargo.toml`
//
//   Inside an archive, flat-vs-nested is decided by the member's path
//   relative to the ARCHIVE's own root, not the archive's position in
//   replacements/. So a `Cargo.toml` at the archive's top level is a
//   FLAT candidate — resolved by basename search across all of
//   target_root — and this workspace has a Cargo.toml per crate, which
//   makes that an immediate hard ambiguity error.
//
//   The fix is not an `overrides::` entry keyed on "Cargo.toml":
//   overrides are checked against bare basenames BEFORE the nested-path
//   check, so that would also capture `benches/abi-return-size/Cargo.toml`
//   and silently collapse both onto the same destination. The archive
//   therefore ships the workspace manifest under a name nothing else can
//   collide with, and the override below is keyed on that name. The
//   bench crate's own Cargo.toml is nested, so its path pins it with no
//   override needed.

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0"
  
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@QUICKFUNCS(
  // Explicit filename -> exact path. Wins outright, no search performed.
  ~target<object>(name, path) { return { name = name, path = path } }
)

@DATA(
  // Repo root. Every nested member of the archive carries its own real
  // path (crates/mid-ecs/src/archetype.rs, benches/abi-return-size/...),
  // so each one pins itself with no search and no ambiguity.
  target_root = "."

  // Documentation that lives in this folder, not content to apply.
  // The manifest itself and any dotfile are always excluded anyway.
  ignore::
    "README.md"

  // The one flat member in the archive. See the note above for why it is
  // keyed on `ROOT_Cargo.toml` and not on `Cargo.toml`.
  overrides::
    target("ROOT_Cargo.toml", "Cargo.toml")
)
